codex
Two requirement-level risks have emerged and I’m validating them against execution now: the proxy plan specifies per-connection inbound/outbound byte budgets that are not present in `limits.ts`, and the profile UI stores a password but appears not to consume it for auto-login. I’m also checking whether the CJK probe can distinguish a missing font from browser fallback rather than merely measuring fallback width.
